    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1394",
      "reading_order": 1805,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.0,
        "t": 285.92,
        "r": 549.7700400000001,
        "b": 250.32999999999993
      },
      "content": "work at an ESD-protected workstation or mat. If an ESD workstation or mat is not available, touch the sheet-metal chassis to provide a static ground before touching an ESD-sensitive assembly. Protect the ESD-sensitive assemblies by placing them in ESD pouches when they are out of the printer.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_1802",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_1",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_1",
          "title": "1. Remove the keyboard."
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_1802",
          "title": "CAUTION:"
        }
      ],
      "page": 149,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "txt_1395",
      "reading_order": 1806,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.00004,
        "t": 240.92000000000007,
        "r": 548.6300400000002,
        "b": 205.32999999999993
      },
      "content": "If the replacement part is a roller or pad, avoid touching the spongy part of it. Skin oils on the roller or pad can cause paper pickup and/or print-quality problems. HP recommends using disposable gloves when handling rollers or pads or washing your hands before touching rollers or pads.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_1802",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_1",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_1",
          "title": "1. Remove the keyboard."
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_1802",
          "title": "CAUTION:"
        }
      ],
      "page": 149,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_1396",
      "reading_order": 1807,
      "section": "CAUTION:",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 144.0,
        "t": 195.91999999999996,
        "r": 541.73,
        "b": 172.32999999999993
      },
      "content": "IMPORTANT: Make sure that all of the shipping materials (for example shipping tape) are removed from the replacement part prior to installation.",
      "section_id": "sec_auto_1802",
      "parent_section_id": "sec_1",
      "section_level": 2,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_1",
          "title": "1. Remove the keyboard."
        },
        {
          "id": "sec_auto_1802",
          "title": "CAUTION:"
        }
      ],
      "page": 149,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
